            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from Baltimore to Norfolk?</h3>
            <p>The train journey typically takes 5 hours 41 minutes to 6 hours 15 minutes, depending on the service and the number of stops.</p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Baltimore to Norfolk?</h3>
            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Northeast Regional, which can complete the journey in approximately 5 hours and 41 minutes with direct service.</p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from Baltimore to Norfolk cost?</h3>
            <p>Ticket prices generally fall between:</p>
            <p><b>$35-$55 for early booking</b></p>
            <p><b>$55-$90 for standard fares</b></p>
            <p><b>$90-$320+ for last-minute or Business Class travel</b></p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Baltimore to Norfolk?</h3>
            <p>Yes, all Amtrak Northeast Regional trains on this route are direct, so there’s no need for transfers.</p>

            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard?</h3>
            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating, Wi-Fi (where available), power outlets, a café car, and luggage space.</p>

            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving?</h3>
            <p>Depending on traffic, driving may take 4-5 hours, while the train is generally stress-free, predictable, and scenic.</p>

            <h3>7. Can you travel from Baltimore to Norfolk in one day?</h3>
            <p>Yes, the route is suitable for same-day trips, but early departures are recommended to maximize time in Norfolk.</p>

            <h3>8. Which station in Baltimore do trains depart from?</h3>
            <p>Most trains depart from Baltimore Penn Station, located in downtown Baltimore. Some airport connections exist but require extra planning.</p>

            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in Norfolk?</h3>
            <p>Trains arrive at Norfolk Station (Harbor Park), conveniently located in the city center and easily accessible by The Tide Light Rail and local buses.</p>

            <h3>10. Is Business Class worth it?</h3>
            <p>Yes, Business Class offers extra legroom, a quieter environment, and priority boarding, making it ideal for travelers seeking more comfort during the 5-6 hour journey.</p>














